# The LOCAL Supabase stack's well-known demo values — committed on purpose, and only these two.
#
# Why committing them is safe, so nobody re-litigates it from the filename: they are the Supabase
# CLI's standard local-dev defaults, identical on every machine that runs `supabase start`. They
# were ALREADY public in this repo before this file existed — ci.yml sets the same two values as
# plain job env ("not a secret — already hardcoded in every e2e spec file"), and the anon key
# appears verbatim in the e2e specs. Nothing here reaches production: Vercel supplies the real
# values via host env, and vite.config.ts refuses a Vercel build that carries this URL.
#
# Vite loads this base file in EVERY mode (dev, test, production build), which is why it is `.env`
# and not `.env.development` — `vite build` runs mode production and Vitest runs mode test, so a
# mode-suffixed file would cover neither. `.env.local` still overrides per-machine (higher
# priority, still gitignored) — that is where real, account-tied keys live (Sentry DSN, Google
# Books key), and they must never move into this file.
#
# This file ends the fresh-worktree failure class: >=5 incidents where a worktree without a
# hand-copied .env.local failed `pnpm build` outright and 17 unit tests, impersonating real
# breakage (AGENTS.md's "fresh worktree" note, 2026-08-19/20 measurements).
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:55321
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZS1kZW1vIiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJleHAiOjE5ODM4MTI5OTZ9.CRXP1A7WOeoJeXxjNni43kdQwgnWNReilDMblYTn_I0
